# tests/change_budget_test.tg — third-audit items 27 (kind-specific contract
# evolution orientation + the zero-delta default-refactor policy), 28
# (semantic sets over counts), 32 (the refactor-equivalence gate), the
# fourth-audit item P0-10 (whole-conjunction contract comparison: one
# verdict per (function, kind), never positional clause pairing) and the
# fourth-audit item P0-19 (the allow-lists are TYPED sets — allowed_api:
# Set[StableDeclId], allowed_abi: Set[StableAbiSurfaceId], allowed_effects:
# Set[AllowedEffect], allowed_capabilities: Set[AllowedCapability],
# allowed_unsafe: Set[StableUnsafeSiteId]; membership never parses a
# rendered row, and untyped delta rows fail closed) end-to-end lanes.
#
# The model itself lives in tg_compiler/change_budget.tg (the ChangeBudget
# record, budget_verify / budget_verified, budget_refactor_default /
# budget_refactor_with_level, EquivalenceRequirement,
# budget_verify_with_equivalence) with the orientation helper in
# tg_compiler/semantic_delta.tg (ContractCompatibility +
# contract_compatibility_of, ContractConjunction +
# contract_conjunction_relation) and the gating ladder in
# tg_compiler/equivalence.tg (equivalence_level_rank,
# equivalence_result_satisfies). This test drives the self-checking lane
# rows:
#   budget_lane_check — T1 precondition strengthening -> violation (T1b
#     the pure-addition form too); T2 postcondition strengthening ->
#     compatible (T2b the pure-addition form); T3 invariant weakening
#     -> violation; T3b precondition weakening -> compatible; T4 the
#     semantic API set allows a specific change while the count cap is 0
#     (the empty-set count fallback rejects); T5 the default-refactor
#     budget rejects any contract delta while the empty delta verifies;
#     T6/T7 the capability / effect sets are primary over their class
#     allow-sets (the empty-set fallbacks reject); T8 the reserved
#     allocation byte budget fails closed (no delta-side byte payload);
#     T9-T15 (item 32) the refactor-equivalence gate — missing result
#     violates, a finite-domain or structural PROOF passes, a
#     TestedNoCounterexample run violates under require_proven = true and
#     passes without a proof demand, Unknown / Counterexample never
#     satisfy, and a higher configured minimum rejects a weaker proof;
#     T16-T21 (P0-10) the whole-conjunction groups — a simultaneous
#     widening pair is accepted under the evolution budget (the
#     positional mis-verdict would reject it), the strengthening twin
#     violates, the opposite-direction audit pair fail-closes as Unknown,
#     an incomparable group violates with the clause ids in the evidence,
#     single-clause behavior is unchanged, and all six clause-order
#     permutations of a three-clause group verdict identically. Every
#     multi-clause row is run in multiple clause orders and must verdict
#     identically.
#   contract_relation_lane_check — the R1-R17 relation + orientation unit
#     rows (R11-R17 pin the ContractCompatibility mapping).
#   contract_conjunction_lane_check — the C1-C9 whole-conjunction unit
#     rows (C2-C4b the simultaneous multi-clause directions, C5 the
#     absence rules, C7 the permutation-invariant model, C8 the
#     single-clause cross-check, C9 the mixed-kind fail-closed guard).
#
# All helpers return mismatch rows (empty = the whole lane verifies).
#
# Run with the repo root as the working directory:
#   tg test tests/change_budget_test.tg

use std::test::assert

use tg_compiler::change_budget::{budget_lane_check}
use tg_compiler::semantic_delta::{contract_relation_lane_check, contract_conjunction_lane_check}

@test
def test_change_budget_contract_evolution_and_sets_lane() -> Unit
  let rows = budget_lane_check()
  assert(rows.len() == 0, "change budget lane mismatches: " + rows.join("; "))
end

@test
def test_contract_relation_and_compatibility_lane() -> Unit
  let rows = contract_relation_lane_check()
  assert(rows.len() == 0, "contract relation lane mismatches: " + rows.join("; "))
end

@test
def test_contract_conjunction_lane() -> Unit
  let rows = contract_conjunction_lane_check()
  assert(rows.len() == 0, "contract conjunction lane mismatches: " + rows.join("; "))
end
